from docx import Document
from docx.shared import Pt,Cm
d=Document()
for s in d.sections: s.left_margin=s.right_margin=Cm(2.5); s.top_margin=s.bottom_margin=Cm(2.3)
st=d.styles['Normal']; st.font.name='Times New Roman'; st.font.size=Pt(11.5)
def P(t,b=False,after=8):
    p=d.add_paragraph(); r=p.add_run(t); r.bold=b; p.paragraph_format.space_after=Pt(after); return p
P("18 October 2026",after=14)
P("The Editor-in-Chief",after=14)
P("Dear Editor,")
P("I submit my manuscript “Beyond Forecast Accuracy: Decision-Centric Evaluation of Demand Forecasting for Inventory Replenishment under Intermittent and Shifting Retail Demand” for consideration as a full research article.")
P("Organisations spend heavily on forecast accuracy, but the business case for that spend runs through inventory decisions. On 3,999 real retail series from the public M5 data I show that the forecaster selected on out-of-sample accuracy, deployed through the standard normal-theory base-stock rule, costs 140.4% more in total inventory cost (95% CI [128.8, 153.4]) than the cost-optimal forecaster–policy pairing, at a lower fill rate. Swapping the forecaster inside that rule is worth 0.4% on the test block (CI [−1.5, +2.5]), while swapping the rule is worth 58.4%.")
P("The paper decomposes the gap and reports an honest tuned baseline: a normal-theory rule tuned on a validation year (safety factor, dispersion refresh, daily (s,S) structure) still costs 25.8% more than the best pairing. It also shows that post-hoc calibrated quantiles raise cost (+21.8%) while a trained quantile model lowers it (−28.9%), and that per-SKU strategy selection, including a gradient-boosted meta-classifier, is counter-productive despite 19.7% oracle headroom. All selection uses a validation year and every number is generated by code that is supplied with the paper. The conclusions hold on an independent sample draw and across ten decision environments.")
P("I believe the work suits your readers because it evaluates forecasting methods by the decisions they support, on the community’s standard retail benchmark, with a fully reproducible pipeline.")
P("The manuscript is original, has not been published, and is not under consideration elsewhere. I am the sole author and approve the submission.")
P("Thank you for your consideration.",after=14)
P("Sincerely,",after=2)
P("Md Ibtashamur Rahman",b=True,after=0)
P("Department of Industrial and Production Engineering",after=0)
P("Shahjalal University of Science and Technology, Sylhet 3114, Bangladesh",after=0)
d.save('cover_letter.docx')
